Thanks to all who replied, especially: Dr Thomas.Blinn, Robert M. Lang
and Chris Medaglia.

I was able to set this value using dxkerneltuner and changing the value
for  max_proc_per_user within the proc subsystem.

Thanks again.

         ---Andy


On Thu, 14 Aug 2003, Andy Malato wrote:

> I have a Personal Workstation running Tru64 5.1A.  When someone
> attempted to login they got a message similar to the following:
>
> max_proc_per_user (=256) exceeded for uid 30525.
>
> What is the proper method to increase this value?  Also, I attempted to
> use sysconfig, but got back an error message:
>
> sysconfig -r proc max_proc_per_user=1024
> max_proc_per_user: attribute does not allow this operation
>
>
> Does resetting this value, if possible, also require a system restart?
>
>
>
