I waited a couple of days to make sure the problem was fixed.
The important part of my original posting is quoted at the end..

I received many suggestions, mostly centered around several config file in
/etc and I opted to alter evmlogger.conf which seemed the most appropriate.
I changed the logging level to warning for most syslog facilities and
removed a few others, leaving nothing reporting below warning.
After a couple of days, I haven't received any other warning messages from
evm and using evmget seems to show the volume being passed to evm to be way
down, which should fix my problem, I think...


> I've been getting messages from the EVM daemon on a fairly new system with
> tru64 5.1b, they come up when the system gets a little busy. It looks like
> it's looking at just about everything being logged via syslog, which can
> amount to quite bit.
> 
> The message says:
> 
> EVM ALERT [600]: EVM daemon: High event activity - exceeds 500 in 10 minutes
> 
> and using:
> 
> evmget | evmshow
> 
> is listing basically all activity from cron, pop, sendmail, ftp.....
> Which I assume is what it calls "events", and obviously when the system gets
> a little busy, it can go over that threshold that triggers the message from
> the evm daemon.

-- 
