We've just migrated to a new HP Alpha box running Tru64 5.1B.  In preparing
for the migration I updated our version of procmail to the latest and
greatest version, 3.22.  The sendmail version is 8.11.1.  Our former Alpha
box had a much older version of both sendmail (pre-8.6) and procmail so I
had to make changes to do the new installation including modifying
src/authenticate.c and setting MAILSPOOLHOME to "/mail/INBOX" so the
default mailbox is ~user/mail/INBOX since this isn't handled by
/etc/procmailrc anymore.

I modified sendmail.cf to include this:

Mlocal, P=/usr/local/bin/procmail, F=SAw5:|/@glDFMPhsfn, S=10/40, R=20/50,
        T=DNS/RFC822/X-Unix,
        A=procmail -Y -a $h -d $u

What baffles me is that some mail is delivered to ~user/mail/INBOX and some
goes to /usr/spool/mail/user.  It doesn't seem to execute /etc/procmailrc
anymore either.  Has anyone else run into a situation like this?  I have
mail piling up where it doesn't belong and I need to get this resolved
quickly.  Thanks.

