We have a problem pertaining to the NFSv3 performance against 
NFSv2, I have seen a lot of other posts discussing the same 
topic , but have not got any satisfatory answers.

Here is my problem.

We have a standalone Alphaserver DS20 running Tru64 v5.1B and 
Patch kit 1 which acts as a NFS server. 

We also have 5 ES40's running v4.0F patch kit 7 running as 
NFS clients. 

Periodically I see the following NFS errors on all of my NFS 
clients

Jul 15 07:47:18 nfsclient vmunix: NFS3 server nfsserver_name 
not responding still trying
Jul 15 07:47:23 nfsclient vmunix: NFS3 server nfsserver_name 
ok


I did a small experiment whereby I copied a 100MB file 
concurrently on all the five NFS clients and I immediately 
get the above error.At this time all my clients were running 
NFSv3.

As a second experiment , I changed my clients to NFSv2 and 
ran the same copy , and surprise I do NOT see any errors, 
Also the the time it takes to copy all the files is one half 
of what it takes with NFSv3.

I have checked the read/write sizes,timeo and retrans values 
on both NFSv2 and NFSv3 and they are the same.

I should also mention that I have Tru64 UNIX v4.0F NFS 
servers and the clients pointing to that server DO NOT get 
the errors.

The above leads me to believe its more of a implementation 
NFS on V5.1B problem.

Has anybody else seen this or know of any solution/fixes?

